```

## Introduction

This Livebook demonstrates how to create and interact with a LiveKit Voice Agent using the Elixir SDK. You'll be able to:

* Configure a voice agent with STT, LLM, and TTS providers
* Connect to a LiveKit room
* Have real-time voice conversations with the AI agent
* Monitor agent performance and metrics

## 🔧 Configuration

First, let's set up all the necessary API keys and configuration:

```elixir
# API Keys Configuration using individual inputs
livekit_url_input = Kino.Input.text("LiveKit Server URL", default: "ws://localhost:7880")
livekit_api_key_input = Kino.Input.text("LiveKit API Key", default: "devkey")
livekit_api_secret_input = Kino.Input.text("LiveKit API Secret", default: "devsecret")
deepgram_api_key_input = Kino.Input.text("Deepgram API Key (for STT)", default: "YOUR_DEEPGRAM_API_KEY")
openai_api_key_input = Kino.Input.text("OpenAI API Key (for LLM and TTS)", default: "YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY")

Kino.Layout.grid([
  livekit_url_input,
  livekit_api_key_input,
  livekit_api_secret_input,
  deepgram_api_key_input,
  openai_api_key_input
], columns: 1)
```

```elixir
# Agent Configuration using individual inputs
room_name_input = Kino.Input.text("Room Name", default: "voice-agent-demo")
agent_name_input = Kino.Input.text("Agent Name", default: "Kelly")
agent_instructions_input = Kino.Input.textarea("Agent Instructions",
  default: """
  You are Kelly, a helpful and friendly AI assistant. You have a great sense of humor and love to help people.
  Keep your responses concise and engaging. You can help with questions, have conversations, and provide assistance.
  """)
